From: retro98boy <retro98boy@qq.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dsi: avoid BLLP power stop on Lenovo Y700 Gen4

Fix visible stripes and repeated interface underruns at 144 and 165 Hz
on the Lenovo Y700 Gen4 NT36536 bonded C-PHY display, allowing the
120 Hz-only restriction to be removed.

With BLLP power stop enabled, both display interfaces repeatedly underrun.
Clearing BLLP_POWER_STOP on both hosts stops the underruns without changing
the mode timings or DSC configuration. Re-enabling it reproduces the fault.

Keep the link active during line blanking on this board. Retain EOF BLLP
power stop for commands during frame blanking, and leave other machines
unchanged. This is a board-specific workaround; the underlying PHY
transition timing difference from downstream is not yet established.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/dsi_host.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/dsi_host.c
@@ -844,8 +844,15 @@
 		/* Always set low power stop mode for BLLP
 		 * to let command engine send packets
 		 */
-		data |= DSI_VID_CFG0_EOF_BLLP_POWER_STOP |
-			DSI_VID_CFG0_BLLP_POWER_STOP;
+		data |= DSI_VID_CFG0_EOF_BLLP_POWER_STOP;
+		/*
+		 * Lenovo Y700 Gen4's NT36536 bonded C-PHY display underruns
+		 * at 144/165 Hz when entering low power during line blanking.
+		 * Keep BLLP active there; EOF BLLP still provides a command
+		 * window during frame blanking.
+		 */
+		if (!of_machine_is_compatible("lenovo,elden"))
+			data |= DSI_VID_CFG0_BLLP_POWER_STOP;
 		data |= DSI_VID_CFG0_TRAFFIC_MODE(dsi_get_traffic_mode(flags));
 		data |= DSI_VID_CFG0_DST_FORMAT(dsi_get_vid_fmt(mipi_fmt));
 		data |= DSI_VID_CFG0_VIRT_CHANNEL(msm_host->channel);
